#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Self-contained construction of a bipartite graph of maximum degree 12 and diameter 5 on 13,122 vertices
(K_{3,3} + doubled matching over Z_27 (controller = a 162-vertex (4,5) bipartite graph, perfect under the fake chart), backtrack-complete per-edge chart fitted to it (diag/fit81.py, seed 91)).  No imports from the repo.

Construction (route-chart lift with a per-edge chart; research/d12D5/EDGECHART.md, research/squads/cells/d12D5.md):
  * Base: 3 + 3 vertices a_i | b_j, 12 edges e = 0..11: [(0, 0), (0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (1, 1), (1, 1), (1, 0), (1, 2), (2, 2), (2, 2), (2, 0), (2, 1)].
  * Controller: voltage lift of the base by Z_27, voltages 0,21,0,0,2,24,0,16,23,24,0,16; 81 + 81 vertices, 4-regular.  CTRL below lists
    its edges (A-vertex, B-vertex, base edge e).
  * Fibre F_3^4.  Every base edge e has its own letter (A_e, b_e) (LETTERS below).  Lift vertex (a, x) is joined to
    (b, A_e x + lam * b_e) for lam in F_3, for every controller edge (a, b, e).  Degree 4 * 3 = 12.
    Order 2 * 81 * 81 = 13,122.
usage: python3 THIS.py out.edges   (apsp.c format: first line n, then one edge "u v" per line)
Vertex numbering: A-vertex (a, x) -> a * 81 + id(x), B-vertex (b, y) -> 6561 + b * 81 + id(y),
id(x) = x0 + 3 x1 + 9 x2 + 27 x3."""
